          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">The Catch: Nearly Every Rival Is Certified</h3>
          <p>
            Here is the catch the label does not tell you. In the November 2026 dataset, almost every certified 35- and 50-pint model from the big appliance brands, including Frigidaire, Midea, Hisense, GE, LG, TCL and Honeywell, sits at exactly 2.01 L/kWh. ENERGY STAR on a mainstream 50-pint unit tells you it meets the bar, not that it beats its rivals. The units worth paying attention to are the ones with an IEF above the floor, which is how the picks in this guide were chosen.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Older Stock Under Version 5.0</h3>
