        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most basements, the AEOCKY LEO-003 is the efficient portable to buy: Most Efficient certification at 2.21 L/kWh, a built-in pump and three years of coverage, for a modest premium over ordinary 50-pint pump units. If you would rather pay less, the Hisense ADH35K26 is the certified value pick for a moderately damp space. For a single room, the Levoit LDH-H251S is the most efficient small unit from a brand most people know, and for a permanent installation, the Aprilaire E080 and Santa Fe Ultra V100 set the efficiency ceiling.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whatever you buy, check the exact model number in the ENERGY STAR product finder, compare integrated energy factor within the same size class, and remember that the humidistat setting and the dampness of the space matter more to your bill than the last tenth of an IEF point.
          </p>
